From: Thingino <dev@thingino.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ipu: match the T31/C100/T40 IPU compatibles again

The 5.15 vendor tree reduced ingenic_ipu_v13.c's of_device_id table to the
single "ingenic,PRJ007-ipu" entry, but the T31 device tree node is
ipu@0x13080000 with compatible = "ingenic,t31-ipu" (the same string the 4.4
T31 SDK driver matched). With no matching compatible the jz-ipu platform
driver never probes, so /dev/ipu is never created. libimp's encoder path
moves each captured frame through that hardware IPU, so without it the
framesource->encoder handoff cannot run (the encoder is never driven and
IMP_Encoder_PollingStream returns rc=-1).

Restore the t31/c100/t40 compatibles that the 4.4 SDK table carried; the
driver body is the same v13 implementation.

--- a/drivers/video/ingenic_ipu/ingenic_ipu_v13.c
+++ b/drivers/video/ingenic_ipu/ingenic_ipu_v13.c
@@ -1286,6 +1286,9 @@
 
 static const struct of_device_id ingenic_ipu_dt_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "ingenic,PRJ007-ipu", .data = NULL },
+	{ .compatible = "ingenic,t31-ipu", .data = NULL },
+	{ .compatible = "ingenic,c100-ipu", .data = NULL },
+	{ .compatible = "ingenic,t40-ipu", .data = NULL },
 	{},
 };
 
